ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":99,"prev":25,"next":101,"titles":103,"firmware":48},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":5,"order":12,"path":13,"context":14,"summary":19,"status":20,"firmware":21,"facts":26,"procedures":54,"parameters":74,"related":75,"body":84,"sources":85,"official_url":30,"controls":93},"fx.overview","Send effects",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11],"fx","send fx","fx types","change fx","effect list","FX I","FX II",0,"knowledge/manual/units/fx/overview.md",{"modes":15,"screens":17},[16],"auxiliary",[18],"M1","Six built-in send effects — chorus, delay, distortion, lofi, phaser and reverb — can be loaded on the two FX tracks, FX I (`T7`) and FX II (`T8`); `M1` of an FX track shows the effect's four controls.","current",{"min":22,"changed_in":23,"guide_version":24,"verified_on":25},"1.0.9",[],"1.1.15",null,[27,32,35,39,44,50],{"id":28,"text":29,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"six","The OP-XY has six built-in send effects — chorus, delay, distortion, lofi, phaser and reverb.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/fx#fx","official",{"id":33,"text":34,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"slots","Two slots hold them, the FX tracks FX I and FX II, which are auxiliary tracks `T7` and `T8`; either slot can take any of the six.",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":38,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"m1","The loaded effect's four parameters sit on the FX track's `M1` page.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/auxiliary#fx-i-and-fx-ii",{"id":40,"text":41,"source":42,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":43},"no-type-cc","No MIDI CC is known that changes the effect type; choose it on the unit.","docs/research/20-midi-control.md#35-auxiliary-tracks-916","community",{"id":45,"text":46,"source":47,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":48,"confidence":49},"list-names","The effect list on the unit spells them chorus, delay, dist, lofi, phaser and reverb.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#213-auxiliary-tracks","1.1.33","verified",{"id":51,"text":52,"source":53,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":48,"confidence":49},"new-project","A new project starts with a delay on FX I, set to a dotted eighth, and a reverb on FX II.","docs/research/30-presets-samples.md#11-a-new-projects-sounds",[55],{"id":56,"goal":57,"preconditions":58,"steps":59,"result":73,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"change","Load a different effect on FX I or FX II",[],[60,61,64,67,70],{"keys":16,"note":25,"set":25},{"keys":62,"note":63,"set":25},"T7/T8","select FX I or FX II",{"keys":65,"note":66,"set":25},"shift + T7/T8","opens the list of effects for that slot",{"keys":68,"note":69,"set":25},"turn E4","scroll to the effect",{"keys":71,"note":72,"set":25},"click E4","pressing `M1` confirms as well","The slot now runs the chosen effect and `M1` shows its parameters.",[],[76,77,78,79,80,81,82,83],"fx.chorus","fx.delay","fx.distortion","fx.lofi","fx.phaser","fx.reverb","auxiliary.fx-sends","mix.levels-pans-sends","Send effects work like the return channels of a mixing desk: tracks send a share of their signal to\nFX I or FX II, and the FX track plays the processed result back into the mix, so one reverb can serve\nevery track. Each slot runs one effect at a time, and FX I can also feed FX II, never the reverse as\nfar as TE documents. The FX tracks themselves — sends, routing, filter, LFO and defaults — are\ncovered with the auxiliary tracks; the units here list what each effect's `M1` encoders do.",[86,88,89,91,92],{"url":30,"kind":87},"guide",{"url":38,"kind":87},{"url":42,"kind":90},"research",{"url":47,"kind":90},{"url":53,"kind":90},[94,95,96,97,98],"key.auxiliary","track.7","track.8","key.shift","encoder.4",{"id":5,"title":100},"Effects",{"id":76,"title":102},"Chorus effect",{"basics.key-notation":104,"basics.main-modes":105,"basics.modules":106,"basics.track-buttons":107,"basics.linked-tracks":108,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":109,"basics.workflow":1